This implementation uses an iterative loop via `4 {…} n` to advance the window of the last four values, avoiding recursion and running in O(n) time with O(1) space.

To compute the `fib4` sequence efficiently without recursion, we use an **iterative approach with constant space complexity** ($O(1)$). This avoids the exponential blowup of naive recursion and the overhead of storing the entire sequence in memory ($O(n)$).

The algorithm maintains a sliding window of the last four values. At each step, it calculates the next value as the sum of these four, shifts the window forward, and repeats until reaching index `x`.

